      "parameters": {
        "promptType": "define",
        "text": "=Guest: {{ $('MockBookingData').item.json.guest_name }}\nVilla: {{ $('MockBookingData').item.json.villa }}\nCheck-in: {{ $('MockBookingData').item.json.check_in }}\nCheck-out: {{ $('MockBookingData').item.json.check_out }}\nPlatform: {{ $('MockBookingData').item.json.platform }}",
        "messages": {
          "messageValues": [
            {
              "message": "**Role:** Senior Guest Relations Specialist and Crisis Manager at a luxury property management company.  **Context:** Our automated n8n pipeline has detected a severe calendar conflict (such as a double-booking or unexpected maintenance) for a newly submitted reservation. We cannot accommodate the guest's request. We must send an immediate, highly professional, and deeply empathetic cancellation/rejection email. The tone must be apologetic, transparent, and solution-oriented to protect the brand's luxury reputation.  **Task:** Write a polite and empathetic rejection email using the provided guest data. You must explicitly: - Address the guest by name and mention the specific villa they attempted to book. - State clearly but diplomatically that due to an unforeseen calendar synchronization error (or prior commitment), their requested dates (check-in to check-out) are regrettably unavailable. - Reassure them that no charges will be processed, or if they booked via a specific platform (like Airbnb or Booking.com), that a full refund process has been initiated immediately. - Offer warm assistance in finding alternative dates or other available properties in our portfolio.  **Target Audience:** Premium guests whose vacation plans are being disrupted. They are likely to be disappointed or frustrated, so they require the utmost respect, empathy, and immediate clarity.  **Input Format:** You will receive the reservation details in JSON format (including guest_name, villa, check_in, check_out, platform).  Output ONLY the final email content. Start strictly with a clear and professional \"Subject: ...\" line, followed by the email body. Use clean formatting with appropriate paragraph breaks. Do NOT output any conversational filler, explanations, or introductory text."
            }
          ]
        },
        "batching": {}
